# Flowers Kitchen — brand rules

Client: Flowers Kitchen, a Jamaican takeaway on St Helen's Street, Ipswich. Run by brothers Asher and Tajay Flowers, cooking recipes taught by their fathers and uncles (born in Jamaica, built a life in Ipswich). Collection only, halal, pre-order available. Food is sold as boxes (jerk chicken, fried chicken, BBQ chicken, curry goat, curry chicken, fried fish, wings), each with rice & peas or white rice, mac & cheese, festival and coleslaw. Business goals: takeaway orders and event catering.

Positioning: "Jamaican family recipes, cooked by the next generation." Premium, warm, trustworthy. Culture through the food, the family and the hibiscus — never flags, palm trees, Rasta stripes, cartoon chefs or street slang.

## Stack
Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind. Mobile-first — most visitors arrive from Instagram on a phone.

## Colour (use these tokens only — no other colours)
| token | hex | use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| cream | #F3EADB | default page background (~60% of any layout) |
| paper | #FBF6EE | cards and raised panels on cream |
| pimento | #2B1B16 | all headings and body text on cream |
| muted | #6E5B4F | secondary text on cream/paper |
| sorrel | #8F1D2C | primary buttons, prices, eyebrows, one hero panel per page max |
| mountain | #1E3A30 | second background: footer, catering section |
| allspice | #B9853F | thin rules, small icons on mountain. Never text on cream |
| hairline | #D9CBB4 | borders and dividers on cream |
On mountain/sorrel backgrounds, text is cream (not white); muted text on mountain is #C9BFAE.
Focus ring: 2px solid mountain on light backgrounds, #D4A55E on mountain.

## Type
- Fraunces (next/font/google, weights 500 & 600) — headlines, prices. Display 64–88px/0.95–1.0, H1 44px, H2 32–40px, H3 22–24px; tighter leading on large sizes. Letter-spacing -0.015em on large sizes. The scale lives in `lib/typography.ts` — use it rather than ad-hoc sizes.
- DM Sans (weights 400, 500, 600) — everything else. Body 17–18px / 1.6.
- Eyebrow: DM Sans 600, 13px, uppercase, letter-spacing 0.32em, in sorrel (#C9BFAE on mountain, with allspice rules — allspice text fails contrast at this size). Put one above every H1/hero headline.
- Buttons: DM Sans 600, 15px, uppercase, letter-spacing 0.08em.
- Never more than two weights per section. No italics except a family quote.

## Layout
- Generous whitespace on an 8px grid: 128px between major sections on desktop, 80px on mobile. Alternate cream and paper backgrounds to separate sections rather than adding borders. If it feels full, remove something.
- Section pattern: eyebrow → heading → short intro → content. Gaps: eyebrow–heading 12px, heading–intro 16px, intro–content 40px. Body text max ~640px wide.
- Shape system — use the tokens in `app/globals.css`, never a hard-coded radius:
  | token | value | use |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `rounded-pill` (`--radius-pill`) | fully round | buttons, nav, chips, toggles, badges, avatar/roundel |
  | `rounded-card` (`--radius-card`) | 16px | cards, panels, sheets, drawers, dialogs |
  | `rounded-input` (`--radius-input`) | 12px | inputs, textareas; photos inset inside a padded card |
  | `rounded-media` (`--radius-media`) | 20px | photos, photo placeholders, maps, the 3D room |
- Borders over shadows. The only shadows are `shadow-soft` (floating header pills) and `shadow-lift` (card hover, sheets). No gradients except a dark overlay on photos for text legibility, and the cream-to-transparent fade behind the scrolled header pills.
- Buttons: one `Button` component — primary (sorrel), secondary (pimento outline), ghost (underline on hover), on-dark (cream outline); md 44px, lg 52px; optional trailing arrow. Never full-width on desktop except in a sheet or card footer.
- Signature detail: short horizontal rules either side of tracked capitals (like the lines around KITCHEN in the logo). Draw them with CSS borders or pseudo-elements, not typed dash characters.
- Motion: fades and 8–16px rises, 300–400ms ease-out. Nothing bounces. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- No third-party embeds or requests on public pages (no cookies but the site's own): maps use the drawn `MapCard`, fonts come from next/font, analytics is cookieless Vercel Analytics. The one exception is Cloudflare Turnstile, loaded only on the catering form's last step. Every absolute URL comes from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` via `lib/site-url.ts`.

## Logo files (in /public/brand/)
- Header: flowers-kitchen_horizontal_full-colour.svg (min 160px wide; below that use the mark).
- Hero/brand moments: flowers-kitchen_primary_full-colour.svg.
- On mountain backgrounds: *_reverse-green.svg. On sorrel: *_reverse-sorrel.svg.
- Favicon/small: flowers-kitchen_mark_full-colour.svg.
- Always alt="Flowers Kitchen". Never recolour, stretch, add effects, or rebuild the logo in CSS/text.

## Copy voice
Warm, proud, plain-spoken. "We" (the family) to "you". British spelling. Short sentences. No emoji, no exclamation marks in headings. Say "boxes", never "meals" or "dishes". Always state plainly near calls to action: Halal · Collection only · Order online (the `serviceNotes` constant in `lib/site.ts`).
Unknowns stay as obvious placeholders: prices "£XX", hours "00:00", founding year "XXXX". Never invent prices, hours, reviews, stats or awards.
Never use em dashes (—) or en dashes (–) in any user-facing text. Use full stops, commas or colons instead, and "to" for ranges. Title separators use "|".

## Accessibility
WCAG AA contrast minimum (the token pairs above pass). Semantic HTML, visible focus states, real alt text, form labels, 44px minimum tap targets.
Focus ring on sorrel backgrounds: 2px solid cream.
